      "side": 1,
      "message": "The WebOb spec for the body parameter says \"If body is a text_type, then it will be encoded using either charset when provided or default_encoding when charset is not provided if the content_type allows for a charset.\" So it seems to me this should be setting the charset to utf-8 and allowing WebOb perform the encoding. Setting the charset has other advantages well because it allows WebOb to have more information when it automatically performs certain operations.",
      "revId": "4fee4a776debd801c4bc276601f99a48b4be6a7c",
