      "side": 1,
      "message": "David, one change I noticed in WebOb 1.7.0 is if there is no body then no Content-Length header is added. Is that the problem you\u0027re trying to solve? I noticed it affects the test_render_response_no_body() test in test_wsgi.py. My understanding is the absence of the Content-Length header is permissible when there is no body. See https://www.w3.org/Protocols/HTTP/1.0/draft-ietf-http-spec.html#Entity-Body.",
      "parentUuid": "1a430d35_0249b35f",
      "revId": "4fee4a776debd801c4bc276601f99a48b4be6a7c",
